---
import GlassLayout from '../layouts/GlassLayout.astro';
---
<GlassLayout
  title="Life in Nepal for Indian MBBS Students — Hostel, Food, Safety | NepalMBBS.in"
  description="What day-to-day life is actually like for Indian MBBS students in Nepal: hostels, food, cost of living, language, safety and travel home."
  path="/life-in-nepal"
>
<div class="tab-pane on" id="pane-lifestyle">
<div class="container">
  <div class="lifestyle-hero rev">
    <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1605640840605-14ac1855827b?fm=webp&w=1920&q=95&fit=crop&auto=format&ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Kathmandu Nepal" loading="lazy">
    <div class="lifestyle-hero-overlay"></div>
    <div class="lifestyle-hero-text">
      <h3>Life in Nepal — Honest Picture</h3>
      <p>Realistic information to help students and parents make informed decisions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  {/* Eight emoji glyphs at font-size:34px (base.css) were the one part of
     this page the gallery's own comment below already flagged as the
     wrong move ("not another row of emoji cards") without actually fixing
     — line icons matching the stroke convention every other icon on the
     site now uses (tab-card, trust-badge, the map), not a second visual
     language. */}
  <div class="life-grid">
    <div class="life-card rev"><div class="life-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.93 4.93l1.41 1.41M17.66 17.66l1.41 1.41M2 12h2M20 12h2M6.34 17.66l-1.41 1.41M19.07 4.93l-1.41 1.41"/></svg></div><h4>Weather</h4><p>Kathmandu: 5–30°C. Pleasant spring/autumn. Cold winters (5–10°C). Monsoon June–August. Similar to North India.</p></div>
    <div class="life-card rev"><div class="life-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M7 2v6a2 2 0 002 2v12M7 2a2 2 0 00-2 2v4a2 2 0 002 2M11 2v20M18 2c-2 0-3 2-3 5s1 4 3 4v11"/></svg></div><h4>Food</h4><p>Indian food widely available in most college hostels. Dal, roti, sabzi available. Indian restaurants in all major cities.</p></div>
    <div class="life-card rev"><div class="life-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 11l9-8 9 8"/><path d="M5 10v10a1 1 0 001 1h4v-6h4v6h4a1 1 0 001-1V10"/></svg></div><h4>Hostel</h4><p>On-campus hostels with separate blocks for male/female students. 24/7 security, Wi-Fi, dining halls at most colleges.</p></div>
    <div class="life-card rev"><div class="life-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2.5" y="6" width="19" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M2.5 10h19"/><circle cx="16.5" cy="14.5" r="1.4"/></svg></div><h4>Monthly Cost</h4><p>Approx ₹15,000–25,000/month covering hostel, food, transport, and personal expenses. Varies by lifestyle.</p></div>
    <div class="life-card rev"><div class="life-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 8.5a16 16 0 0120 0M5.5 12.5a11 11 0 0113 0M9 16.5a6 6 0 016 0"/><circle cx="12" cy="20" r="1" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></div><h4>Connectivity</h4><p>Indian SIM cards work in Nepal with roaming. Affordable local SIMs available. Good internet in colleges and cities.</p></div>
    <div class="life-card rev"><div class="life-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="8.5" cy="8" r="3"/><path d="M2.5 20v-1a6 6 0 0112 0v1"/><path d="M16 4.2a3 3 0 010 5.6M19.5 20v-1a5.99 5.99 0 00-3.5-5.46"/></svg></div><h4>Community</h4><p>Large Indian student community at all major Nepal medical colleges. Cultural events, student associations, peer support.</p></div>
    <div class="life-card rev"><div class="life-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="13" rx="2.5"/><path d="M3 11h18M7 17v2M17 17v2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="14" r="0.9" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/><circle cx="16.5" cy="14" r="0.9" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></div><h4>Transport</h4><p>Direct buses from Gorakhpur/Delhi (Sonauli border). Flights Delhi→Kathmandu available. No visa for Indian citizens.</p></div>
    <div class="life-card rev"><div class="life-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3l7.5 3.2v5.3c0 5-3.2 8.4-7.5 9.5-4.3-1.1-7.5-4.5-7.5-9.5V6.2z"/><path d="M12 9v6M9 12h6"/></svg></div><h4>Healthcare</h4><p>Good hospitals in Kathmandu and Pokhara. Indian students have access to college hospital facilities during studies.</p></div>
  </div>
  {/* A real photo gallery, not another row of emoji cards — the page's
     own subject is what day-to-day life looks like, and eight abstract
     icons said nothing about that. Reuses `.why-img`'s already-built
     treatment (rounded corners, hover zoom, gradient overlay, badge) so
     this doesn't invent a second image-card language for one page.
     Asymmetric three-up rather than equal thirds, on purpose — three
     identical columns is the layout every generic template reaches for
     first. Falls back to a tokened gradient automatically if any of
     these fail to load (chrome.js's `.img-broken` handler). */}
  <div class="life-gallery rev">
    <div class="why-img life-gallery-lg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544735716-392fe2489ffa?fm=webp&w=1920&q=95&fit=crop&auto=format&ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Kathmandu valley and the Himalayan foothills" loading="lazy"><div class="why-img-overlay"></div><div class="why-img-badge">🏔️ Kathmandu Valley</div></div>
    <div class="why-img"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1553856622-c4f04ea9b6df?fm=webp&w=1400&q=95&fit=crop&auto=format&ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Prayer flags and Nepali street life" loading="lazy"><div class="why-img-overlay"></div><div class="why-img-badge">🙏 Everyday Nepal</div></div>
    <div class="why-img"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544736150-6e4617d64a3b?fm=webp&w=1400&q=95&fit=crop&auto=format&ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Momos and Nepali street food" loading="lazy"><div class="why-img-overlay"></div><div class="why-img-badge">🥟 Local Food</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="curr-wrap rev">
    <div class="curr-title">💱 INR ↔ NPR Currency Converter</div>
    <div class="curr-row"><span class="curr-lbl">INR ₹</span><input class="curr-in" type="number" id="inr-val" value="10000" data-act="input" data-do='[["convertCurr","inr"]]' inputmode="numeric"></div>
    <div class="curr-row"><span class="curr-lbl">NPR रू</span><input class="curr-in" type="number" id="npr-val" value="16000" data-act="input" data-do='[["convertCurr","npr"]]' inputmode="numeric"></div>
    <div class="curr-result" id="curr-result">₹10,000 = रू 16,000</div>
    <div class="curr-note">*Approx rate: 1 INR ≈ 1.6 NPR. Verify current rate at xe.com before any transaction.</div>
  </div>
</div>
</div>

<style>
  /* base.css's .life-icon{font-size:34px} was sized for an emoji glyph;
     the line icons above need their own box instead of an inherited
     font metric. Same rest/hover colour shift as .tab-svg elsewhere
     (var(--g-ink-3) -> var(--brand)) so this reads as the same icon
     system, not a second one. */
  .life-icon {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    margin: 0 auto 12px;
    color: var(--g-ink-3);
    transition: color var(--d-2, 0.15s) var(--ea-out, ease);
  }
  .life-icon svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  .life-card:hover .life-icon { color: var(--brand); }
</style>
</GlassLayout>
